{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And in the morning and you shall see.</b> Not concerning the glory of which it is said ״וְהִנֵּה כְּבוֹד יְהוָה נִרְאָה בֶּעָנָן״ is this said, but thus He said to them: In the evening you shall know that it is in His power to grant your desire, and He will give meat — but He will not give it with a shining face, because you asked Him improperly and with a full belly; and the bread that you asked for out of need — in its descent in the morning you shall see the glory of the light of His countenance, for He brings it down to you in love, in the morning, when there are hours to prepare it, with dew above and dew below, as though set in a קֻפְסָא (Yoma 75)." "<b>Your murmurings against YHWH.</b> Like that which is against." "<b>And we — what.</b> What are we reckoned?" "<b>For you murmur against us.</b> That you make everything boil over against us — and your sons and your wives and your daughters and the mixed multitude. And perforce I must explain תַּלִּינוּ in the causative (hiph'il) voice because of its dagesh and its reading, for if it were weak (rafeh) I would explain it in the reflexive (hitpa'el) voice, like ״וַיָּלָן הָעָם עַל מֹשֶׁה״ (Exodus 17), or if it were dageshed and had no yod and were read תִּלּוֹנוּ, I would explain it in the sense of תִּתְלוֹנְנוּ. Now as it stands it means: you make others murmur, like with the spies — ״וַיַּלִּינוּ עָלָיו אֶת כָּל הָעֵדָה״ (Numbers 14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:43.127914871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}